# Environment files (M19.13). The blanket `.env*` pattern also matched
# `.env.example`, which is documentation the project ships and a reader copies
# to `.env.development`/`.env.local`. Only the local copies are ignored, and the
# negation re-includes the template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
